.nh
.TH "PB-PORT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-port - Name machine ports and set a machine's front desk


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb port [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Name machine ports for private browser addresses and choose where unnamed addresses of a
machine go. Names live on the server and work on every computer of everyone allowed
the port; they never grant access to a port.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for port


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-port-front-desk(1)\fP, \fBpb-port-name(1)\fP
